Fix in that last block: remove the stray `</DialogFooter>` — the closing order is `</DialogFooter></DialogContent></Dialog>`.

Two things worth knowing about these classes. First, `backdrop-blur-xl` only shows through if your `DialogOverlay` is translucent — set it to `bg-slate-950/60` rather than a solid color, otherwise the blur is invisible. Second, the emboss effect depends on stacked `inset` shadows, so if you add `overflow-hidden` to a tile you'll clip the glow div but keep the bevel; that combination is intentional in `MetricTile`.

I wrote these against the standard shadcn `Dialog` API without inspecting your project, so verify your `DialogContent` doesn't already hard-code conflicting `bg-*` or `rounded-*` defaults — if it does, the local classes may lose to it depending on class order, and you'd want `cn()` merging via `tailwind-merge`.
